DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       yyuuyy22ttooppaamm  reads  raw  YUY2  bytes as input and produces a PAM image as
       output.  The input file is just YUY2 bytes.  You have  to  specify  the
       width and height on the command line, since the program obviously can't
       get them from the file.

       The output image has maxval 255.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common  Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), yyuuyy22ttooppaamm recognizes the
       following command line options:




       --wwiiddtthh=_w_i_d_t_h
              Width of the image, in pixels.  This must be an even number.


       --hheeiigghhtt=_h_e_i_g_h_t
              Height of the image.



       These options are mandatory.


